From 0d153ec5775a18046fec485ddee4707eba806442 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:41:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a live process's never-acked notice claim no
 longer blocks the chat's owner forever [daveey]

t_01a199de3003e911: the completion of t_01a197b1039901c3 never reached chat 20261026_235722_bef6c6. The live
`hermes dashboard` (pid 44404) held an in-flight marker on the sub (203961 -> 204381) it never acked; the owning
serve could not claim while a LIVE process held it, and the dashboard, refused SESSION_NOT_OWNED every 5 min,
rewound only its latest range and kept the earlier marker. Nine more rows on that pid were stuck the same way.

- claim_unseen_events_for_sub: a live foreign holder no longer blocks when its held range has no deliverable
  event left (new `deliverable_kinds`; tui passes the kinds that render a notice) or its claim is older than
  NOTIFY_CLAIM_STALE_S (15 min, new `inflight_at` column; a legacy NULL is dated by the newest event it holds).
  It is rewound like an orphan, with a WARNING.
- release_notify_claim: a refused non-owner (SESSION_NOT_OWNED) and a stopping poller hand back their WHOLE
  marker for each sub they no longer buffer, so the owner claims on its next tick.
- Why 4, the leaks: the unloaded sweeper returned without an ack for a silent-only claim (unblocked/archived);
  the live poller dropped a silent claim whose ack was skipped behind an earlier pending claim, and
  _kb_mark_delivered / _kb_rewind_refused dropped durable claims not yet acked. Each now acks or keeps them.
- ack_notify_claim returns whether it cleared/moved the marker.
